---
import CustomImage from "../components/mdx/CustomImage.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout path="/about" title="About" description="About JonLuca DeCaro">
  <div class="text-page reading-column mb-8">
    <h1 class="clear-both mt-0 mb-2 text-2xl leading-tight font-semibold uppercase">About</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Hi! I'm JonLuca DeCaro. I currently work at <a href="https://openai.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenAI</a>.
        Prior to that, I was a founder of <a href="https://weights.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Weights</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also built <a href="https://deckexport.com/">DeckExport</a>, a free tool for saving supported public document
        and presentation links as PDFs, with page preview and selection. Its
        <a href="https://deckexport.com/tools/google-pdf-link-generator">Google PDF-link generator</a> creates native
        Docs, Slides and Sheets export links, individually or in batches.
      </p>
      <CustomImage
        alt="JonLuca DeCaro"
        src="/images/profile.webp"
        class="mx-auto max-w-[20rem]"
        width={1161}
        height={1161}
        loading="eager"
        fetchPriority="high"
      />
      <h2>New here?</h2>
      <p>
        If you're new here, these three posts are a good place to start. They're representative of what I like writing
        about: technical rabbit holes, reverse engineering, product systems, and odd corners of the internet.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <a href="/posts/illegal-streams?ref=about">Illegal streams, decrypting m3u8's, and building a better stream experience</a>
          {" "} - A look at illegal sports streams, how they piggyback real services, and what it took to build a better viewing client.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/posts/deobfuscating-amex-scammer?ref=about">Obfuscated javascript, scam emails, and American Express</a>
          {" "} - Reverse-engineering obfuscated JavaScript from scam emails and tracing the campaign back to its command-and-control server.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/posts/ryan-air?ref=about">Ryanair, Hamiltonian Cycles, and using graph theory to find cheap flights</a>
          {" "} - Using graph theory to plan a cheap European trip through Ryanair's network, then turning the idea into a tool other people can use.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>You can also <a href="/feed.xml">subscribe to the blog via RSS.</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
